The Tempest Lord is the neutral elite of the Stormcaller. Its Rain lasts the
whole battle, its spells hit harder, and at the top rank Lightning strikes
every foe in its target's row.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Endless rain   its Rain lasts the whole battle
  35 Rolling storm  +20% spell damage
  40 Storm thrift   spells cost 15% less mana
  45 Full fork      the second foe takes all of Lightning's damage
  50 Tempest        +20% spell damage
  55 Deep reserves  +25% maximum mana
  60 Storm wall     Lightning also strikes every other foe in its target's
                    row

It needs the Stormcaller first (<ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] tempest-lord confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Shaman talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves (+10% maximum mana),
Spell Edge (+10% spell damage), Focused Will (blows break your chant 25% less
often). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
